        {
          "id": "exponential-and-division",
          "claim": "By [F3], $1+x\\le\\exp(x)$; both sides are nonnegative, so [F4] gives $(1+x)^m\\le(\\exp(x))^m=\\exp(mx)=\\exp(d)=e^d$. Since $x^d=(d/m)^d>0$ by [F6], divide step 1.1 by this quantity to obtain the stated bound.",
