        "notes": "Independently read all five proof steps, 19 supplier interfaces and Alquier Lemma 2.2 with its proof (PDF pp.12–13). The local partition-KL version is proved directly, without assuming equivalence to density KL: boundedness gives integrability and positive finite exponential integral; log-sum on a finite level-set partition gives the finite-valued inequality. Deterministic finite-range approximants have uniform error <=1/n; expectation modulus and multiplicative exp bounds give additive log error <=1/n, so finite KL passes to the limit. Infinite KL is explicitly vacuous; zero prior partition mass implies zero posterior mass, and zero posterior terms are omitted. Constant functions and singleton partitions are valid, an empty probability space is impossible, and no choice or diagram is needed. Reader/post source hashes authenticate the analytic-prerequisite repair; no finding remains."
