        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-7",
        "notes": "Read all five steps and 23 supplier interfaces, current Hoeffding MGF proof, and Alquier Theorem 2.1 with complete proof (PDF pp.12–13). For C>0, unit-range MGF at t=-lambda*C/m and finite independent factorization produce exp(lambda^2*C^2/(8m)); C=0 is separate, with KL>=0 from the one-cell partition. Product-measurable bounded loss licenses Tonelli, giving a positive finite measurable M_lambda. Markov defines one event independent of rho; change of measure applies pointwise on it to bounded f_S, so all absolutely continuous posteriors are covered together without taking a potentially nonmeasurable uncountable union. Positive lambda division and finite/infinite KL conventions are correct. Checked m=1, C=0, degenerate losses, delta endpoints excluded, and fixed-prior/fixed-lambda qualifications; only posterior averages are asserted. No choice or diagram is required."
      }
