          "source": "def-product-sigma-algebra-and-finite-product-sigma-algebras",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $(X,\\mathcal A)$ and $(Y,\\mathcal B)$ be measurable spaces. Their\n**product sigma-algebra** is\n\n$$\\mathcal A \\otimes \\mathcal B := \\sigma(\\{A \\times B : A \\in \\mathcal A,\\ B \\in \\mathcal B\\}),$$\n\nthe sigma-algebra on $X \\times Y$ generated by the measurable rectangles of\nMeasurable rectangles in a product of measurable spaces.\n\nFor the empty family, put $\\prod_{i<0}X_i:=\\{()\\}$ and define its **empty\nproduct sigma-algebra** by\n\n$$\\bigotimes_{i<0}\\mathcal A_i:=\\{\\varnothing,\\{()\\}\\}.$$\n\nFor a nonempty finite family of measurable spaces $(X_i,\\mathcal A_i)$ with\n$i<n$, the **finite product sigma-algebra** is defined recursively by\n\n$$\\bigotimes_{i<1}\\mathcal A_i := \\mathcal A_0,\\qquad \\bigotimes_{i<n+1}\\mathcal A_i := \\left(\\bigotimes_{i<n}\\mathcal A_i\\right)\\otimes\\mathcal A_n.$$\n\nThis recursive definition is the finite base case used later when the library\npasses to countable product constructions.",
