            "step 1.1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "finite-union-bound",
          "claim": "There are exactly $\\binom{m}{i}$ subsets of $[m]$ of size $i$ by [F6]. Applying [F5] over all such subsets and then over $i=0,\\ldots,d$ yields $\\Pr_{D^m}\\left(\\bigcup_{I\\subseteq[m],\\,|I|\\le d}E_I\\right)\\le\\sum_{i=0}^{d}\\binom{m}{i}(1-\\epsilon)^{m-i}$, which is the stated bound. The output of any consistent compression learner is one of these reconstructed candidates, so its measurable failure event is contained in this union.",
