        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-7",
        "notes": "Read every proof step, all 14 supplier interfaces and Floyd–Warmuth Theorem 5 (printed p.279) with full Appendix proof (pp.302–303). Fixed I gives a jointly measurable disagreement indicator; Tonelli makes selected-tuple risk measurable. Coordinate permutation preserves the finite product law by rectangle uniqueness. With selected coordinates fixed, remaining consistency is A_s^(m-i), of mass (1-r_i(s))^(m-i); m>d ensures positive exponent, so r_i>epsilon bounds it by (1-epsilon)^(m-i). Dropping selected consistency only enlarges the event; finite subset counting and union bound prove the stated stronger existence event. Checked i=0,d=0,m=1, repeated observations, zero/one risk and m=d+1. No uncountable union, conditional-probability regularity assumption, side information or choice is used. Reader touched only the F1 contract quotation; source is exactly unchanged from pre/post."
