          "source": "cor-exponential-reciprocal-and-positivity",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For every real $x$, $\\exp(x)>0$ and\n$$\\exp(-x)=\\frac1{\\exp(x)}.$$",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "1.2"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "zero-compression-case",
          "claim": "If $d=0$, [F1] reduces the bad-subset probability to $(1-\\epsilon)^m$. By [F3] this is at most $\\exp(-m\\epsilon)$, which is at most $\\delta$ when $m\\epsilon\\ge\\log(1/\\delta)$ by [F4].",
