          "id": "risk-calculation",
          "claim": "Every $A(s)$ has ten points, so [F1] gives $R_D(h_{A(s)})=10/20=1/2$. Since $A(s)$ is disjoint from the sample support, every sampled label is predicted as zero and $\\widehat R_s(h_{A(s)})=0$.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "F1",
            "step 1.1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "zero-kl-and-bound-violation",
          "claim": "The measures $\\pi_s$ and $\\rho_s$ are equal, so every finite-partition divergence is zero and [F2] gives $\\mathrm{KL}(\\rho_s\\|\\pi_s)=0$. By [F4], $\\log4\\le3$, and therefore the proposed right side is at most $20/(8\\cdot10)+3/20=2/5<1/2$. Thus the displayed inequality fails for every sample.",
          "step": "3.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F2",
            "F4",
            "step 1.1",
            "step 2.1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
