      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-7",
        "notes": "Read all four proof steps and eight cited supplier interfaces including the logarithm upper-bound proof. Every length-10 sample on 20 points leaves at least 10 unseen points; lexicographic finite selection is total and measurable. Its selected hypothesis has exactly 10 errors in 20 population points and no sample errors, including samples with repeats. Equal prior/posterior point masses give zero KL for every partition. At m=10,lambda=20,delta=1/4 the RHS is <=1/4+3/20=2/5<1/2, so failure probability is one. Absolute continuity holds pointwise; only the fixed-prior requirement fails. No AC or diagram; the example is local, while Alquier supplies the valid fixed-prior theorem."
