          "claim": "For $m\\ge3$, the size parameter satisfies $m>d=2$. At $\\epsilon=1/4$, step 2.1 shows that the event $R_D>\\epsilon$ is exactly the all-zero sample event, hence has probability $2^{-m}$. Its value is at most $(3/4)^m$, which is the $i=0$ term in the sum in [F3]; all other terms are nonnegative. Thus the exact example probability is bounded by $\\sum_{i=0}^{2}\\binom{m}{i}(3/4)^{m-i}$ as stated.",
          "step": "3.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F3",
            "step 2.1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        }
      ],
