        "notes": "Read all three verification steps and four cited supplier interfaces. On any labeled sequence the first occurrence of each of two inputs gives a total deterministic finite discrete encoder selecting at most two entries; arbitrary inconsistent labels still define a total encoder/reconstructor, and target-consistent sequences reconstruct all observed labels. Empty sample consistency is vacuous. For m>=3 risk is 1/2 precisely on the all-zero sample, otherwise zero (an unseen zero gets the correct default). Independence gives 2^-m; this is <=(3/4)^m, the i=0 term of the nonnegative sum. Checked all-zero/all-one/mixed samples, m=3 and zero sample for the scheme. Source bytes are unchanged pre/post; only the exact F1 definition quote was enriched. No choice or diagram."
